course: dictionary
lesson: 7373
title: Plesiosaurs: sea reptiles, not dinosaurs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A plesiosaur was a large sea reptile that lived at the time of the dinosaurs. It had a broad body, four flippers and often a very long neck. Plesiosaurs are now extinct, which means none are alive today.
explain: We know about them from fossils, the hard remains or traces of animals that lived long ago. «Plesiosaurs were sea reptiles with four flippers that died out 66 million years ago.» So a fossil is our evidence, not a living animal we can watch.
explain: Plesiosaurs are often mistaken for dinosaurs, but they were not. They lived at the same time as the dinosaurs, yet they swam in the sea. «So the flying pterosaurs and the swimming plesiosaurs, mosasaurs and ichthyosaurs were not dinosaurs, even though they lived at the same time.»
explain: Scientists check their ideas against evidence. Mary Anning found one of the first complete plesiosaur skeletons on the coast at Lyme Regis in England. The Loch Ness Monster may look like a plesiosaur in pictures, but there is no evidence that it is real. Always ask: what does the evidence show?
fact: A plesiosaur was a large sea reptile with a broad body, four flippers and often a very long neck.
fact: Plesiosaurs are extinct: they died out about 66 million years ago.
fact: Plesiosaurs were not dinosaurs, though they lived at the same time as them.
fact: A fossil mother with a baby inside shows that plesiosaurs gave birth in the sea.
fact: Mary Anning found one of the first complete plesiosaur skeletons on the coast at Lyme Regis in England.
exercise: «A plesiosaur had four flippers and often a very long neck.» How many flippers did a plesiosaur have? | Six | *Four | Eight | Two
exercise: «Plesiosaurs are now extinct.» What does extinct mean? | Living in the sea today | Found in a cave | *No longer alive anywhere on Earth | Very large
exercise: A pupil says plesiosaurs were dinosaurs. What is the right answer? | Plesiosaurs were flying animals | *Plesiosaurs were not dinosaurs; they were sea reptiles that lived at the same time | Plesiosaurs were dinosaurs that lived on land | Plesiosaurs were dinosaurs because they lived at the same time
test: How do we know about plesiosaurs today? | *From fossils | From films and cartoons | From the Loch Ness Monster | Because someone saw one swimming last year
test: «Plesiosaurs were sea reptiles with four flippers that died out 66 million years ago.» What does this tell us? | They still live in the deep sea | *They lived in the sea and are now extinct | They lived on land only | They were dinosaurs that flew
exam: Where did Mary Anning find one of the first complete plesiosaur skeletons? | The Sahara Desert | Paris, France | Loch Ness in Scotland | *Lyme Regis in England
